{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They band together</b> — from the root גדוד." "<b>And condemn innocent blood</b> — the meaning: when he has been slain, that the wicked killed him, the discerning will consider him a man of death, guilty and wicked; therefore he was put to death. This the poet says on his behalf and on behalf of the whole congregation of Israel."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:17.467438387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}